  <div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">A COMMUNITY AND ITS SHELTER</p><p>This original English retelling follows <strong>Bhagavata Purana, Book 10, chapters 24–27</strong>. It begins with a question about worship and follows the episode through the storm, the villagers’ wonder and Indra’s reconciliation. Conversations and descriptions are condensed.</p></div>
  <section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl>
    <div><dt>Krishna</dt><dd>The young cowherd whose divine protection shelters Vraja.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Nanda</dt><dd>Krishna’s father in Vraja and an elder of the cowherd community.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The people and cattle of Vraja</dt><dd>The community caught in the storm.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Indra</dt><dd>The celestial ruler whose anger gives way to humility.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Govardhana</dt><dd>The hill worshipped by the community and lifted as its shelter.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Surabhi</dt><dd>The divine mother of cows who honours Krishna after the storm.</dd></div>
  </dl></section>
